<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace Drupal\Tests\my_module\Functional;

use Drupal\Tests\BrowserTestBase;
use PHPUnit\Framework\Attributes\Group;
use PHPUnit\Framework\Attributes\RunTestsInSeparateProcesses;

/**
 * Tests the my_module dashboard page.
 */
#[Group('my_module')]
#[RunTestsInSeparateProcesses]
class DashboardPageTest extends BrowserTestBase {

  /**
   * {@inheritdoc}
   */
  protected static $modules = ['my_module'];

  /**
   * {@inheritdoc}
   */
  protected $defaultTheme = 'stark';

  /**
   * The user account used to view the dashboard.
   */
  protected ?AccountInterface $dashboardUser = NULL;

  /**
   * {@inheritdoc}
   */
  protected function setUp(): void {
    parent::setUp();

    // Adjust the permission to whatever my_module.routing.yml requires on the
    // my-module/dashboard route.
    $this->dashboardUser = $this->drupalCreateUser(['access my_module dashboard']);
  }

  /**
   * Tests that the dashboard returns 200 and renders its title text.
   */
  public function testDashboardPage(): void {
    $this->drupalLogin($this->dashboardUser);
    $this->drupalGet('/my-module/dashboard');

    $this->assertSession()->statusCodeEquals(200);
    $this->assertSession()->pageTextContains('Dashboard');
  }

  /**
   * Tests that a user without the permission is denied access.
   */
  public function testDashboardAccessDenied(): void {
    $this->drupalLogin($this->drupalCreateUser());
    $this->drupalGet('/my-module/dashboard');

    $this->assertSession()->statusCodeEquals(403);
  }

}
```

Add the `use Drupal\Core\Session\AccountInterface;` import alongside the others if you keep the typed property.

A few notes on the choices:

- **Functional, not Kernel or Unit.** The route is an HTTP endpoint returning rendered markup, so it needs a booted site and a real request. A Kernel test can't make HTTP requests, and a Unit test would require mocking the whole container.
- **`#[RunTestsInSeparateProcesses]`** is a hard requirement on Drupal 11.3 and strongly recommended on 10.x.
- **Namespace and directory** must match exactly: `Drupal\Tests\my_module\Functional` at `tests/src/Functional/`, or the runner won't discover the class.
- **The permission string is a placeholder.** I don't know what `my_module.routing.yml` declares on that route. If the route uses `_access: 'TRUE'` or `_permission: 'access content'`, drop the custom permission and the second test method, or swap in the real one. If you paste your routing YAML I'll correct it.
- **Second test method** covers the most likely error path. Delete it if the page is genuinely public.

